🔹 Step 4: Optimize Step by Step

Here’s how you learn optimization by doing hands-on:

File Format Optimization

Convert CSV → Parquet (columnar, compressed):

df.write.mode("overwrite").parquet("taxi_parquet")
df_parquet = spark.read.parquet("taxi_parquet")


Partition Pruning

Partition by a frequent filter column (e.g., tpep_pickup_datetime by year/month):

df = df.withColumn("year", col("tpep_pickup_datetime").substr(1,4))
df.write.partitionBy("year").parquet("taxi_partitioned")


Reduce Shuffle Partitions
Default is 200. Adjust based on dataset & cluster:

spark.conf.set("spark.sql.shuffle.partitions", "50")


Caching
If reusing a DataFrame multiple times:

df.cache()
df.count()  # materializes cache


Broadcast Joins
If joining with small reference tables:

from pyspark.sql.functions import broadcast
result = df.join(broadcast(dim_table), "id")


Skew Handling

If passenger_count has skew (e.g., most rows = 1), use salting or spark.sql.adaptive.enabled=true.

